// The old output listed the keys sorted, `"asdf": 5, "qwer": 7, "rtyu": 6`, the order its host's map
// kept them in. A map here keeps its keys in the order they were first added, as a set keeps its
// elements.
@test
MUTABLE_MAPS()
    corpus("mutable_maps")

// The old output printed each constructor as its host object, `RecordConstructor(num, num,
// List(Symbol(v)))`. Here a constructor prints as its declaration names it, `<constructor num(v)>`.
@test
NESTED_BLOCK_DECLARATION()
    corpus("nested_block_declaration")

